  phenotype  and so whilst i've specifically included  two examples that include cd38  cd38 is emerging as a key enzyme  involved in inflammation  antenescence which could be also helping  to link nadplus  metabolism and its decline all of the  different hallmarks of agent  in particular because we know that there  are senescent cells in the brain and  that in itself has been linked to  alzheimer's disease so it's all a matter  of trying to put the puzzle pieces  together  but the more important question is if we  know that this is the case and nad plus  is really important  what strategies are there to increase  nad plus levels  well if we consider the analogy whereby  water  is an 80 plus then there are three main  ways in which you can maintain  the water levels in a sink firstly is to  prevent any leakages  and loss of water in this case  representing the different enzymes that  consume nad plus  for example cd38 then there's the fact  that you want to increase the supply of  water  that can come from precursors to nad  plus  and then the third strategy is to open  up the forceps to allow the flow of  water  to be stronger and this could come by  activating different enzymes involved in  the metabolism  and generation of nad plus or as i like  to think of it  the make break or take strategies to  prevent nad plus decline  so let's start with the taking  strategies ways of supplementing nad  plus levels  since that's why we have a majority of  information at the moment  one option would be to supplement with  nicotinamide  since it can be converted back to nad  plus by the salvage pathway  however at the moment the consensus  seems to be that at high levels  nicotinamide seems to be acting as a  feedback inhibitor  of nad plus dependent enzymes including  parps and sertoins  an alternative idea is to use niacin  which is actually  already commonly found in multivitamins  however there seems to be some concerns  with niacin in terms of high doses  in particular be